The project code itself is WTFPL licensed

Below are the libraries i used

SDL2, SDL2_image, SDL2_mixer and SDL2_ttf
    zlib license.
    https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/main/LICENSE.txt (this is SDL3 license but it will do i guess)
    Some files from SDL2 are in this repo as i extracted them from the 
    MINGW32 development package so Windows builds are a little less petty. 

GLEW
    BSD-3-Clause and MIT (GL, EGL and GLX headers have copyrights from Khronos and Mesa). 
    The original license is at glew/LICENSE.txt.
    https://glew.sourceforge.net/

libGLU from Mesa3D
    SGI Free Software License B v2.0 (MIT-style).
    https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/glu
    I only use some functions from libutil. When thinking of OpenGL library for Windows
    And Linux compatibility i was only able to come up with Mesa (it's really great software)
    I only compile libGLU as compiling mesa3d on Windows is as hard as it sounds

glvnd
    MIT license. Only the headers under glvnd/include are used when compiling libGLU
    https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glvnd

Cabin font (assets/fonts/Cabin-Regular.ttf)
    SIL Open Font License 1.1. Designed by Pablo Impallari.
    https://github.com/impallari/Cabin

Original SourceBox recreation
    MIT License. Programmed in Python by Sierra (programmer1o1).
    I heavily referenced their code for some things, so MASSIVE props to them :)
    https://github.com/programmer1o1/SourceBox